Yep, you named that one wand rather than maple wands in general.

If you use #name on that (or most other unidentified objects), it should
first ask "Name an individual object?"  Apparently, you answered with a
"y" for that particular maple wand.  If you answer "n" instead, you will
get a "What do you want to call? ..." prompt at which you can select
that wand.  It will then prompt "Call a maple wand:", to which you can
answer with a title you want to apply to all maple wands.  That title
will show up after "called" in your "\" discoveries and your inventory
(much like the "water" and "fire water" entries you already seem to have
for a couple potions).
